Myth: In a quiet harbor where sails whispered secrets to the quay, there stood a bell that rang not with time but with intention. Its clapper was a small boy named Lio, who carried a pocketful of borrowed chances. When a passerby paused long enough to choose kindness over certainty, the bell tolled softly and a thread of light stretched from the bell into the heart of the city, lifting small weights of hesitation from every doorway.

